<title>FRANCE: Elf considers floating Isis unit - paper.</title>
<headline>Elf considers floating Isis unit - paper.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-05-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>French oil major Elf Aquitaine and the Institut Francais du Petrole (IFP) are considering selling their stakes in oil services holding company Isis on the stock market, newspaper Le Figaro said on Friday.</p>
<p>The value of holdings in Isis was estimated at between three and four billion francs, the report said. IFP holds 57 percent in Isis, Elf holds 39 percent through its Sogelfa unit, and BNP owns four percent. Isis paid out 45 million francs in dividends last year, it said.</p>
<p>A flotation would allow Elf to continue its divestment from the oil services sector and value IFP's holding.</p>
<p>No comment was available from Elf or IFP.</p>
<p>Isis holds 12 percent in Technip, 17 percent in Geophysique, 20 percent in Coflexip, 50 percent in Procatalyse and 35 percent in Geoservices, the report said.</p>
</text>
